{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780329365,"nonce":"/UOty6+L9N8ktttT+IYFnE2O6tg=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEBC1LA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/201","origin":"github"},"title":"Deployment 2026-06-01: clean survey run — override/resume (#52) + turning limits + cross-track","message":"## Purpose\n\nThe next on-water run should be the **clean survey run** that several navigation items have been waiting on — [#173](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/173) (2026-05-26) and [#186](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/186) (2026-05-28) were both collision-avoidance / dense-buoy days, not sustained clean survey lines, so a cluster of nav changes is still field-untested.\n\n**Headline new validation:** the **override-based mid-survey repositioning** work — [unh_marine_navigation #52](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/52) / [PR #53](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/53), merged 2026-06-01. Updatable hover + goto overrides, and mid-line resume after an override. **Sim-validated 2026-06-01**; needs on-water confirmation.\n\n## Must-verify this deployment\n\n### Override / resume — PRIMARY ([unh_marine_navigation #52](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/52) / [PR #53](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/53))\n\n- [ ] **Updatable hover (park)** — re-issue a hover override at a new spot while it's parking → boat re-parks at the *new* spot, not the original.\n- [ ] **Updatable goto (nudge)** — re-issue a goto override while it's driving → boat re-targets to the *new* point (does not latch on the original).\n- [ ] **Mid-line resume** — mid survey line, hover-park OR goto-nudge (e.g. ~10 m back to recover a sonar hiccup), then cancel / let it complete → the survey **resumes from the boat's current position**, NOT a transit back to the line start + full re-run. *(This is the hiccup-recovery workflow the change was built for.)*\n- [ ] **Mission re-send mid-line** ([unh_marine_navigation #35](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/35) family) — operator Executes a *different* trackline mid-line → boat follows the new line. Class-significant; students will redirect the boat mid-mission.\n\n### Survey-dependent nav items (blocked on a clean run)\n\n- [ ] **Turning limits** (#124 §2 / PR #172) — run a survey pattern with apron turns; confirm helm yaw cap 1.0 rad/s + planner min turning radius 1.5 m behave on tight apron turns. Still untested — prior deployments had no clean apron turns.\n- [ ] **Cross-track / line-following characterization** ([#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164)) — sustained clean lines; capture `pid_state` (cross-track error) and characterize the undulation (~1.6 m median RMS observed; SE-asymmetry unconfirmed). Exclude collision-stop / re-acquisition stretches. *(Cross-track capture also added sim-side: [unh_marine_simulation #63](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_simulation/pull/63).)*\n- [ ] **Hover stop-point projection** ([unh_marine_navigation #33](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/33) / [PR #34](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/34)) — confirm hover settles into station without overshoot on engagement.\n- [ ] **TF extrapolation on multi-line survey goals** ([unh_marine_navigation #23](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/23)) — watch for TF-lookup-out-of-time errors during survey patterns; verify whether still occurring.\n\n### Operator awareness\n\n- [ ] **Survey-line avoidance overlay + followed path on the operator station** ([#199](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/199) / [PR #200](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/200), merged 2026-06-01) — confirm the overlay + the boat's followed path render on CAMP.\n\n## ⚠️ Watch out for\n\n1. **Mid-line resume threshold.** Resume-from-position relies on the boat reading as \"on the line\" (`RobotOnPath`, 5 m cross-track tolerance). If a survey runs lines closer than ~5 m apart, a resume could match the wrong line — tune the threshold in `run_tasks.xml` if so. Not expected at typical survey spacing.\n2. **Goto auto-completes; hover holds.** A goto override drives to the point and then the survey resumes — it does NOT hold there. To hold at a nudged spot, use a hover override.\n3. **Cross-track artifacts.** Large XTE excursions during collision-stops / line re-acquisition are artifacts, not line-following quality — characterize undulation only on clean, uninterrupted stretches.\n\n## 🔧 Data capture\n\n- Boat-side bag already records `pid_state` (cross-track error) — confirm it's capturing on the survey run for offline cross-track / undulation analysis.\n\n## Operators\n\n- Roland + Claude Code Agent (Claude Opus 4.8, 1M context)\n\n## Hosts in use\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub)\n- **mercat** — boat-side Windows / QINSy host (if a survey phase is reached)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Date TBD** — set the title date when the deployment firms up. Activate with the workspace `/start-deployment` skill (`.agents/deployment.yaml`).\n- **In flight / not yet landed:** reactive corridor path-adjuster ([unh_marine_navigation #51](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/51), #30) — fold its validation in here if it merges before this run.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}